     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>After Ganpati Visarjan, Mumbai Cleaned Dadar Beach</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#CivicSenseRevolution</span> <span>#DadarBeach</span> <span>#MumbaiBeachCleanup</span> <span>#WasteToWorth</span></div>
       <p>Mumbai recently demonstrated a powerful display of community spirit, transforming the aftermath of Ganpati Visarjan into an inspiring act of civic responsibility. Following the festivities, over 100 Mumbaikars gathered at Dadar Beach, joining hands with The Better India's Civic Sense Revolution initiative. Their collective effort resulted in the removal of more than 2,000 kg of waste left behind after the idols had departed.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/after-ganpati-visarjan-mumbai-cleaned-dadar-beach.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This significant clean-up operation, which commenced at 8 AM, showcased the tangible impact of community action. Participants worked diligently to clear the sands, embodying a commitment to environmental stewardship. The collected waste is set to undergo a remarkable transformation. With the assistance of Beach Warrior Chinu Kwatra, these materials will be repurposed into school benches, providing valuable resources for underprivileged children. This initiative exemplifies how a community can come together, turning waste into something truly useful and embodying what civic sense looks like in practice. It's a testament to the idea that even after celebrations, the commitment to a cleaner environment and a better future persists, turning a clean-up into an act of profound civic contribution and social upliftment.</p><p>Why it matters: This initiative highlights the power of community action to address environmental challenges and create lasting social good.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the source material without any errors.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/videos/after-ganpati-visarjan-mumbai-cleaned-dadar-beach-12582444" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
