     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Alisha Chinai Reveals Behind-the-Scenes Trivia for Iconic 'Kajra Re'</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Alisha Chinai</span> <span>#Kajra Re</span> <span>#Bunty Aur Babli</span> <span>#Bollywood Music</span></div>
       <p>Singer Alisha Chinai recently shared previously unknown details about the creation and recording of the popular song ‘Kajra Re’ from the 2005 film 'Bunty Aur Babli'. During a conversation with Komal Nahta, Chinai recounted several fascinating anecdotes surrounding the track.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/alisha-chinai-reveals-behind-the-scenes-trivia-for-iconic-ka.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Chinai revealed that she was contacted at the eleventh hour to lend her voice to the song. She recalled having to rush from Alibaug to make it to the recording session, highlighting the last-minute nature of her involvement. The urgency underscored the rapid pace often encountered in film music production.</p><p>She also disclosed that the legendary lyricist Gulzar penned the distinctive 'alaap' section of the song in a remarkably short span of ten minutes. This detail offers insight into the spontaneous creative genius behind one of Bollywood's most enduring item numbers.</p><p>Chinai further mentioned that the makers had initially informed her that ‘Kajra Re’ was conceived as an item song, with the possibility of Aishwarya Rai Bachchan performing it. She also praised Aishwarya Rai's appearance in the song, describing her as looking &quot;like a GODDESS.&quot; These revelations provide a glimpse into the collaborative process and the artistic vision that brought the memorable track to life.</p><p>What to watch: Further interviews with artists revealing untold stories from Bollywood's musical history.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively synthesizes the trivia provided in the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/alisha-chinai-shares-fascinating-kajra-re-trivia-i-was-called-at-the-last-minute-i-rushed-from-alibaug-gulzar-wrote-the-alaap-in-10-minutes-says-aishw/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
