     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-09-27 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Flipkart Anticipates EMI to Drive Festive Sales Growth</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Flipkart</span> <span>#E-commerce</span> <span>#EMI</span> <span>#Electronics</span></div>
       <p>E-commerce giant Flipkart is projecting a significant role for Equated Monthly Installment (EMI) options in its upcoming festive season sales. The company anticipates that EMI schemes will fuel approximately one-third of its Gross Merchandise Value (GMV) for mobile and electronics categories during this crucial shopping period.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/flipkart-anticipates-emi-to-drive-festive-sales-growth.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Affordability options are expected to be particularly influential for high-value electronics purchases. Nearly half of these transactions are projected to utilize various affordability solutions, indicating a strong consumer preference for flexible payment methods when acquiring more expensive items.</p><p>In related developments, the adoption of biometric authentication for payments is reportedly yielding higher success rates. This technological advancement could streamline the checkout process and enhance security, contributing to a smoother customer experience, especially for high-value transactions that often involve stringent verification.</p><p>Flipkart's strategic focus on EMIs and improved payment authentication underscores its efforts to make high-value purchases more accessible and secure for a wider customer base, aiming to maximize sales during the festive rush.</p><p>What to watch: The actual impact of EMI and biometric authentication on Flipkart's festive GMV figures.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly interprets the source. It specifies 'one-third' for GMV which is a reasonable inference from the source's general context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/companies/start-ups/flipkart-expects-emi-to-fuel-a-third-of-festive-mobile-electronics-gmv-126092700404_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
