     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Gyanesh Kumar's Political Journey Under Scrutiny Amidst New Label</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Gyanesh Kumar</span> <span>#CEC</span> <span>#Kerala Politics</span> <span>#BJP</span></div>
       <p>Gyanesh Kumar is currently at the center of a significant row, drawing attention to his career trajectory. A recent report highlights the scrutiny surrounding his past affiliations and present perceptions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/gyanesh-kumars-political-journey-under-scrutiny-amidst-new-l.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Throughout his career, Kumar was notably recognized for his ability to navigate the complex political landscape of Kerala. He was once described as a &quot;go-to man&quot; for both the Congress and Left parties in the state, adept at working with the oscillating LDF and UDF governments. This demonstrated a capacity to operate effectively across differing political spectrums.</p><p>More recently, however, a contrasting label has emerged, identifying him as a &quot;BJP man in Delhi.&quot; This shift in perception has prompted observers to question whether this current classification represents a full circle in a career marked by adaptability.</p><p>The ongoing &quot;SIR row&quot; brings these differing characterizations to the forefront, inviting discussion on the evolution of his public and political image. His journey from a figure who successfully engaged with various political entities in Kerala to being associated with a specific national party is now a point of focus.</p><p>What to watch: The ongoing discussions surrounding Gyanesh Kumar's political identity.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source summary and maintains a neutral tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/all-the-gyaneshs-men-from-go-to-man-for-cong-left-in-keralam-to-bjp-man-in-delhi-life-comes-full-circle-for-cec-ws-klrt-10355626.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
