       <h1>India Enters Day 8 of Asian Games 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Asian Games</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Sports</span></div>
       <p>India continues its campaign at the 2026 Asian Games as the event reaches its eighth day. The focus shifts to the squash courts, where Abhay Singh and Anahat Singh are slated to compete in their respective final matches for the men's and women's singles events.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/india-enters-day-8-of-asian-games-2026.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>As the competition intensifies, the Indian contingent remains in the spotlight with high expectations for these final-stage performances. The squad has been active throughout the week, maintaining a presence across various disciplines as the games progress toward their conclusion.</p><p>The upcoming matches represent a critical juncture for the Indian athletes involved in the singles brackets. Supporters and sports analysts are monitoring these events closely as the athletes look to secure their final rankings in the competition. The ongoing updates reflect the broader participation of the Indian team in the 2026 edition of the Games.</p><p>What to watch: The results of the men's and women's singles squash finals.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly identifies the athletes and the context provided in the source.</p>
