       <h1>Indian Women's Fotball Team To Make Historic Kolkata Debut Against Russia</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Indian Women's Football</span> <span>#Kolkata Debut</span> <span>#Russia</span> <span>#Friendly Matches</span></div>
       <p>The Indian women's national football team is poised for a significant and historic moment as they prepare to play their first-ever international matches in Kolkata. The team is scheduled to host Russia for two friendly encounters, marking a notable debut for women's football in the city.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/indian-womens-fotball-team-to-make-historic-kolkata-debut-ag.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>These anticipated matches will be held at the Kishore Bharati Krirangan, providing a new venue for the national side. The first fixture is set for October 8, with the second friendly match following just three days later on October 11. Both games are strategically scheduled within the FIFA women's international match window, ensuring their official status and allowing for optimal team preparation and player availability.</p><p>This occasion is particularly significant for the Indian women's team, offering them a chance to compete on a fresh home ground and connect with a passionate football audience in Kolkata. The selection of the city for these high-profile international friendlies against Russia highlights its importance as a burgeoning hub for football. The team will undoubtedly aim to deliver strong performances and leave a lasting impression during this inaugural series.</p><p>What to watch: The Indian women's team's historic performance in Kolkata and their engagement with local fans.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly synthesizes the source information regarding the upcoming matches in Kolkata.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/football/indian-womens-fotball-team-to-make-historic-kolkata-debut-against-russia-12105789#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
