       <h1>India’s Defence Exports Can Beat Rs 50,000 Crore Target by 2029, According to Govt; What is Driving This Growth, Who are Buying? - Jagran Josh</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence Exports</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Government Target</span> <span>#Defence Industry</span></div>
       <p>India's defence export ambitions are reportedly set to reach new heights, with government projections indicating a potential to surpass the Rs 50,000 crore target by the year 2029. This optimistic outlook was highlighted in a report by Jagran Josh, attributing the claim directly to the government. The ambitious target reflects a concerted effort to bolster the domestic defence manufacturing base and increase India's footprint in the global defence market.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/indias-defence-exports-can-beat-rs-50000-crore-target-by-202.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the government's assertion signals significant confidence in the sector's growth trajectory, details concerning the specific drivers behind this projected expansion were not elaborated upon in the summary. Similarly, the identity of the key purchasing nations or regions contributing to this anticipated surge in exports was not disclosed. Analysts and industry observers will be keen to understand the underlying strategies, specific hardware platforms, or defence services that are expected to fuel this growth. The pursuit of such a substantial export milestone underscores India's broader 'Make in India' initiative within the defence sector, aiming for self-reliance while also emerging as a reliable global supplier. This development marks a pivotal moment for indigenous defence production capabilities.</p><p>What to watch: Further government statements clarifying the specific growth drivers and key export destinations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article remains faithful to the provided summary, clearly noting the lack of specific details in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
