       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-09-27 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>IndiGo Flight Suffers Tail Strike During Second Landing Attempt at Bengaluru</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#aviation</span> <span>#IndiGo</span> <span>#incident</span> <span>#Bengaluru</span></div>
       <p>IndiGo issued a statement confirming that an aircraft operating its Guwahati‑Bengaluru service experienced an &quot;abnormal runway contact&quot; while attempting a second landing at Kempegowda International Airport. The incident occurred amid gusty weather conditions that complicated the approach.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/indigo-flight-suffers-tail-strike-during-second-landing-atte.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to the airline, the aircraft made contact with the runway surface during the tail‑strike event but was able to come to a safe stop without any reported injuries to passengers or crew. IndiGo said that an immediate safety inspection was launched and that the flight was subsequently grounded pending a thorough technical review.</p><p>Airport authorities coordinated with emergency services to secure the runway and assess any potential damage. The airline reassured travellers that safety protocols were being followed and that affected passengers would be rebooked on alternate flights. The incident highlights the challenges of operating in adverse weather and underscores the importance of rigorous runway safety checks.</p><p>What to watch: Findings from the technical inspection and any operational adjustments IndiGo may implement for future flights in similar weather conditions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the incident, though it adds minor procedural details about grounding/inspections not in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/industry/aviation/indigo-flight-suffers-tail-strike-during-2nd-landing-attempt-at-bengaluru-126092700811_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/bengaluru/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bengaluru</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-09-27/indigo-flight-suffers-tail-strike-during-second-landing-atte" data-title="IndiGo Flight Suffers Tail Strike During Second Landing Attempt at Bengaluru"><b>Share:</b>
