       <h1>‘Iran ready for doomsday war’, FM Araghchi says</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Iran</span> <span>#diplomacy</span> <span>#conflict</span> <span>#Middle East</span></div>
       <p>Iran's Foreign Minister, Abbas Araghchi, has issued a stark warning, stating that Iran is prepared for war to resume. The Foreign Minister's comments underscore a heightened state of readiness within the nation, indicating a firm stance on potential future conflicts. He specifically noted that Iran is prepared 'even if it comes to a doomsday war,' a phrase that conveys the extreme gravity of the country's defensive posture.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/iran-ready-for-doomsday-war-fm-araghchi-says.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Minister Araghchi's statement reflects a significant declaration from a high-ranking Iranian official regarding the nation's military and diplomatic readiness. Such declarations are closely monitored by international observers for insights into regional stability and geopolitical tensions. The readiness to confront a 'doomsday war' suggests a comprehensive assessment of potential threats and a resolve to respond with full force if necessary.</p><p>The Foreign Minister's remarks, as reported, serve as a clear communication of Iran's position on its defence capabilities and its willingness to engage in conflict. This public assertion of preparedness is a key element in Iran's diplomatic and security messaging to both regional and international audiences.</p><p>What to watch: Further statements from Iranian officials and international reactions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately conveys the content and tone of the Foreign Minister's statement as reported in the source.</p>
