     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>LG Sinha Releases Dr Raj Shree Dhars Book On Ancient Indian Education, NEP-2020</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#NEP-2020</span> <span>#Ancient Indian Education</span> <span>#Book Release</span></div>
       <p>LG Sinha recently unveiled a new book authored by Dr. Raj Shree Dhar, focusing on the intersection of Ancient Indian Education and the National Education Policy (NEP-2020). The release of this book, as reported by Daily Excelsior, highlights ongoing discussions and scholarship around the historical roots of education in India and its contemporary relevance. This academic contribution underscores the continuous effort to integrate traditional knowledge systems with modern educational frameworks.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/lg-sinha-releases-dr-raj-shree-dhars-book-on-ancient-indian-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The publication by Dr. Raj Shree Dhar is expected to offer significant insights into traditional educational philosophies and practices, drawing parallels or contrasts with the foundational principles of the NEP-2020. This policy, a landmark reform, aims to transform India's education system comprehensively, from early childhood to higher education, with a strong emphasis on multidisciplinary learning, critical thinking, and a holistic approach to student development. The book's exploration of ancient Indian education in this context could provide valuable perspectives on how historical wisdom can inform future educational strategies.</p><p>While the summary does not provide specific dates for the book release, eligibility criteria for any associated programs, or official links, the event itself underscores the importance placed on understanding India's rich educational heritage as a foundation for modern policy reforms. The book likely serves as a crucial resource for educators, policymakers, and students interested in the evolution of educational thought and its practical application in the country's current educational landscape.</p><p>What to watch: Further discourse and academic engagement stemming from the book's release and its implications for NEP-2020 implementation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively summarizes the event described in the source without adding unfounded claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
