     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mumbai Promotes Artificial Ponds for Sustainable Ganpati Visarjan</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#GanpatiVisarjan</span> <span>#Mumbai</span> <span>#ArtificialPond</span> <span>#BMC</span></div>
       <p>The Brihanmumbai Municipal Corporation (BMC) is championing a sustainable shift in how Mumbai celebrates Ganesh Chaturthi. By promoting the use of artificial ponds for Ganpati Visarjan, the city is offering devotees a practical and respectful alternative to traditional sea immersion. This initiative aims to maintain the sanctity of the festival while significantly reducing the environmental impact on natural water bodies.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/mumbai-promotes-artificial-ponds-for-sustainable-ganpati-vis.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Traditionally, idol immersion has often led to debris and broken idols washing up along shorelines. Artificial ponds provide a controlled environment that ensures the ritual is completed with full devotion while protecting the city's coastal ecosystem. This shift reflects a growing civic consciousness, balancing long-standing traditions with the urgent need for environmental responsibility. As the city prepares for the festivities, the BMC's approach highlights that modern urban living can successfully integrate ecological preservation with cultural heritage. By choosing artificial ponds, citizens are participating in a collective effort to keep Mumbai’s waters clean while honoring their faith.</p><p>Why it matters: This transition demonstrates how civic authorities and citizens can collaborate to preserve cultural traditions while actively protecting urban natural resources.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the provided source summary regarding BMC's initiative.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/videos/lifestyle/no-sea-visarjan-mumbai-promotes-artificial-ponds-12580970" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
