     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NDTV Defence Summit 2026: Rajnath Singh, Military Chiefs To Take The Stage — Check Full Schedule, Timings - NDTV Profit</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence Summit</span> <span>#Rajnath Singh</span> <span>#Military Chiefs</span> <span>#NDTV</span></div>
       <p>The NDTV Defence Summit 2026 is gearing up to be a pivotal event for India's strategic community, as confirmed by NDTV Profit. The summit will host Defence Minister Rajnath Singh and the nation's Military Chiefs, who are slated to address the gathering. This high-level participation highlights the summit's role as a significant forum for discussions on national security and defence policies. The convergence of such prominent figures offers a crucial platform for exploring the evolving challenges and opportunities within the defence sector.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/ndtv-defence-summit-2026-rajnath-singh-military-chiefs-to-ta.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the preliminary announcement did not detail specific hardware procurements, ongoing programmes, or particular agency initiatives, the involvement of the Defence Minister and top military brass indicates a focus on broader strategic themes. Such events typically facilitate an exchange of views on defence preparedness, technological advancements, and geopolitical dynamics impacting India. The summit's schedule and precise timings, which are expected to be released, will offer further insights into the specific topics slated for discussion. The gathering of these key decision-makers is anticipated to provide valuable perspectives on the nation's defence posture and its future strategic direction, fostering dialogue among stakeholders. The summit serves as a public-facing platform to underscore the government's commitment to robust defence.</p><p>What to watch: The overarching strategic insights and potential policy signals emanating from the high-level addresses.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately summarizes the provided source information without overstepping.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
