     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NEET PG 2026 Candidates Allege Score Discrepancies, AIMSA Appeals to Health Minister</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#NEET PG</span> <span>#Medical Education</span> <span>#Score Discrepancies</span> <span>#AIMSA</span></div>
       <p>Candidates who appeared for the NEET PG 2026 examination have raised serious allegations regarding discrepancies in their scores. This development has prompted the All India Medical Students' Association (AIMSA) to officially address the matter with the Union Health Minister.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/neet-pg-2026-candidates-allege-score-discrepancies-aimsa-app.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The concerns expressed by the NEET PG 2026 aspirants highlight potential issues within the examination's evaluation process. These allegations point to a need for a thorough review of the scoring system to ensure fairness and transparency for all candidates.</p><p>AIMSA's decision to write to the health minister underscores the gravity of the situation and the collective demand from the student community for intervention and resolution. The association is advocating for a clear explanation and appropriate action concerning the alleged discrepancies.</p><p>The allegations have sparked significant concern among the medical student fraternity, emphasizing the importance of accurate and consistent scoring in high-stakes examinations like NEET PG. The outcome of AIMSA's appeal to the health minister is eagerly awaited.</p><p>What to watch: The response from the health ministry and any subsequent actions taken regarding the alleged score discrepancies.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source information regarding the NEET PG 2026 allegations.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
