     <article class="story single" data-beat="science">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · Phys.org · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NEET with a disability: What's holding back visually impaired young people who want to work</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#disability</span> <span>#workforce</span> <span>#vision impairment</span> <span>#longitudinal study</span></div>
       <p>A long-term research project has tracked the life paths of 80 young people with vision impairment over an 11-year period. The study followed participants as they transitioned from their school years into adulthood, aiming to understand the challenges they face in the workforce.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/neet-with-a-disability-whats-holding-back-visually-impaired-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Researchers engaged with the participants at regular intervals throughout this decade-plus timeframe. By monitoring their progress, the study sought to document what aspects of their personal and professional journeys were successful and which areas required improvement.</p><p>The findings center on the experiences of these individuals as they navigate the transition to independent adult life and employment. By speaking directly with the participants, the research highlights the factors that either support or hinder their ability to secure and maintain work.</p><p>This study provides an longitudinal view of the obstacles encountered by visually impaired youth, offering insight into systemic or personal barriers that persist after formal education ends. The goal remains to identify clear opportunities for better support structures during this critical life stage.</p><p>What to watch: Future policy recommendations based on the long-term outcomes of these 80 participants.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source material without introducing any fabricated information.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://phys.org/news/2026-09-neet-disability-visually-impaired-young.html" rel="noopener">Phys.org</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-09-27/neet-with-a-disability-whats-holding-back-visually-impaired-" data-title="NEET with a disability: What's holding back visually impaired young people who want to work"><b>Share:</b>
