     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>New RBI Rules for Bulk Fixed Deposits from October 1: What Savers Need to Know</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#RBI</span> <span>#Fixed Deposit</span> <span>#Bulk Deposit</span> <span>#Interest Rates</span></div>
       <p>From October 1, 2026, new regulations from the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) will come into effect, altering how banks manage and disclose interest rates for bulk fixed deposits (FDs). These changes are primarily aimed at enhancing transparency and consistency for larger depositors.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/new-rbi-rules-for-bulk-fixed-deposits-from-october-1-what-sa.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>For an ordinary saver, these rules might not directly impact your typical small to medium-sized FDs, as &quot;bulk deposits&quot; usually refer to larger sums, often above a certain threshold set by the RBI. However, understanding these changes is beneficial if you consider making a substantial deposit in the future.</p><p>Under the new guidelines, banks will be required to disclose their bulk deposit interest rates daily. This means that if you are considering a large FD, you should expect more frequent updates on available rates, allowing for more informed decisions.</p><p>Furthermore, the rules mandate consistency in bulk deposit rates across all branches of a bank. This ensures that the interest rate offered for a bulk FD should be uniform, regardless of which branch you approach. There may be specific exceptions, particularly those related to liquidity regulations, which depositors should be aware of before committing to a bulk FD.</p><p>What to watch: How these changes affect transparency and competition among banks for large deposits.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a clear and accurate summary of the new RBI rules for bulk deposits as per the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/fd-rules-change-from-1-october-what-depositors-should-know-about-bulk-deposit-rates-11790469926484.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
