       <h1>Pakistan Ranks Highest on Global Terrorism Index 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Pakistan</span> <span>#Terrorism</span> <span>#Global Terrorism Index</span> <span>#Husain Haqqani</span></div>
       <p>Pakistan has been identified as the nation most significantly affected by terrorism, according to the Global Terrorism Index 2026. This ranking highlights a persistent challenge for the South Asian country. The index, which assesses the impact of terrorism across various nations, placed Pakistan at the top of its list for the upcoming year.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/pakistan-ranks-highest-on-global-terrorism-index-2026.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The findings prompted a sharp reaction from former envoy Husain Haqqani. He commented on the situation via X, attributing the country's predicament to a policy of &quot;keeping 'snakes in backyard'.&quot; This statement suggests a critical view on past or present strategies concerning extremist elements within the region.</p><p>The Global Terrorism Index is a comprehensive study that analyzes trends and patterns in terrorism worldwide. Its 2026 report draws attention to the severe consequences experienced by Pakistan, underscoring the human and geopolitical costs associated with terrorism. The report's methodology typically involves assessing factors such as the number of terrorist incidents, fatalities, injuries, and property damage.</p><p>Haqqani's remarks, while succinct, reflect a sentiment that has often been voiced by observers regarding the complexities of combating terrorism, particularly when internal policies are perceived as contributing factors. The former envoy's use of a vivid metaphor underscores the gravity of the situation as seen from his perspective.</p><p>What to watch: The implications of this ranking on Pakistan's international relations and internal security policies.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the provided source information without introducing unverified claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
