     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Powerful Nor’easter Batters US Northeast; Over 100,000 Without Power</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#US Northeast</span> <span>#Nor'easter</span> <span>#Weather</span> <span>#Power Outages</span></div>
       <p>A powerful nor’easter swept across the US Northeast on Sunday, bringing a host of severe weather conditions that significantly impacted the region. The storm, characterized by its intense winds and heavy precipitation, led to widespread coastal flooding, affecting numerous communities situated along the Atlantic seaboard.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/powerful-noreaster-batters-us-northeast-over-100000-without-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The adverse weather system resulted in extensive infrastructure disruptions. Over 100,000 residents were left without power as the storm battered utility lines and equipment. Travel across the Northeast was also severely affected, with reports of delays and cancellations impacting roads and potentially public transportation networks. Commuters and travelers faced considerable challenges throughout the day.</p><p>Forecasters had previously warned of the nor'easter's potential severity and continued to issue alerts regarding the ongoing threat of tidal flooding. These warnings underscored the persistent danger posed by elevated water levels, even as the storm's core began to move away. Emergency response teams and utility crews were actively engaged in addressing the immediate consequences of the storm, working to restore services and assist affected populations. The full assessment of the storm's impact and the subsequent recovery efforts are expected to continue in the days ahead.</p><p>What to watch: The timeline for full power restoration and the potential for residual tidal flooding.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source summary without adding extraneous or unbacked details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/powerful-noreaster-batters-us-northeast-over-100000-without-power-ws-l-10355947.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
