     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rajnath Singh Affirms India's Commitment to Security and Strategic Autonomy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#National Security</span> <span>#Foreign Policy</span></div>
       <p>India's Defence Minister, Rajnath Singh, has affirmed the nation's steadfast resolve to protect its security and strategic autonomy in the face of any threats. Speaking on the matter, Singh underscored India's commitment to maintaining its independent foreign policy and defence posture, as reported by DD India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/rajnath-singh-affirms-indias-commitment-to-security-and-stra.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The statement emphasizes a core principle of India's defence doctrine, which prioritizes national interests and the ability to make sovereign decisions without external coercion. This assertion by Minister Singh highlights the government's stance on safeguarding its territorial integrity, national assets, and broader strategic objectives.</p><p>Strategic autonomy is a key tenet for India, allowing it to navigate complex geopolitical landscapes and forge partnerships based on its own assessments and requirements. The declaration signals that any perceived threat to this autonomy or the nation's security will be met with decisive action to uphold these fundamental principles.</p><p>Minister Singh's remarks serve as a clear communication of India's defence policy, reinforcing its position on the global stage. It reiterates that the nation is prepared to take necessary measures to preserve its sovereignty and ensure the well-being of its citizens. The statement, attributed to Rajnath Singh, conveys a strong message of national resilience and determination.</p><p>What to watch: Further official statements or policy developments related to India's security and strategic autonomy.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately attributes the stance to the official mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
