       <h1>Rohit Sharma-Virat Kohli Eye Several Milestones Ahead Of 1st ODI Against West Indies</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Rohit Sharma</span> <span>#Virat Kohli</span> <span>#ODI</span></div>
       <p>Thiruvananthapuram is preparing to host a significant cricketing event as India commences its One Day International series against West Indies. The opening match will place a spotlight on two of India's most prominent cricketers, Rohit Sharma and Virat Kohli, who are set to begin their pursuit of several major milestones. Both players, now established as 'ODI-exclusive legends,' are expected to command considerable attention as they aim for career-defining records.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/rohit-sharma-virat-kohli-eye-several-milestones-ahead-of-1st.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The first India-West Indies ODI is anticipated to be a crucial platform for Sharma and Kohli to initiate their chase for these significant achievements. These potential milestones are projected to dominate cricketing headlines, generating widespread discussion and anticipation in the lead-up to the 2027 ICC Cricket World Cup. Their individual quests add an intriguing dimension to the upcoming series.</p><p>As the Men in Blue take the field, the focus will extend beyond the team's collective performance to the individual accomplishments of this iconic duo. The records they are targeting and their continued impact on the game are considered vital aspects that could influence narratives and generate excitement leading into the next global tournament. The Thiruvananthapuram fixture therefore holds enhanced importance as the starting point for these aspirations.</p><p>What to watch: The start of Rohit Sharma and Virat Kohli's chase for significant ODI milestones.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source summary regarding the upcoming ODI series and the focus on the milestones of the two players.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
