       <h1>Sikandar Raza's son smashes 279 off 146 balls with 20 sixes in U14 50-over game in Bulawayo</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Sikandar Raza</span> <span>#Eesa Butt</span> <span>#Under-14 Cricket</span> <span>#Bulawayo</span></div>
       <p>Bulawayo witnessed an extraordinary display of batting prowess recently, as Eesa Butt, the son of Zimbabwe's T20I captain Sikandar Raza, unleashed a record-breaking innings in an Under-14 50-over game. Playing for Hellenic Academy U14, Butt smashed an astounding 279 runs off just 146 deliveries against CBC U14.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/sikandar-razas-son-smashes-279-off-146-balls-with-20-sixes-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The young cricketer's monumental effort was punctuated by a remarkable 20 sixes, showcasing immense power and timing beyond his years. This incredible feat took place on September 26, 2026, in Bulawayo, leaving spectators and coaches alike in awe of the talent on display. The innings single-handedly dominated the scorecard, providing a clear indication of his potential.</p><p>Eesa Butt's performance immediately drew comparisons to his illustrious father, Sikandar Raza, known for his explosive batting and all-round capabilities on the international stage. While still in the early stages of his cricketing journey, this innings has firmly placed young Butt in the spotlight, hinting at a promising future in the sport. The sheer volume of runs scored at such a rapid pace in a 50-over format is a testament to his skill and temperament.</p><p>What to watch: Eesa Butt's continued development in junior cricket and his trajectory towards higher levels.</p>
       
