     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Sitaare Zameen Par: Aamir returns to Japanese theatres</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#AamirKhan</span> <span>#SitaareZameenPar</span> <span>#JapaneseRelease</span> <span>#Bollywood</span></div>
       <p>Bollywood superstar Aamir Khan is slated for a significant return to Japanese cinemas with his upcoming film 'Sitaare Zameen Par', scheduled for release in spring 2027. This event marks a notable moment for his Japanese fanbase, as it will be his first theatrical release in the country since the highly successful 'Dangal' premiered back in 2018. The extended gap highlights the anticipation surrounding this new project.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/sitaare-zameen-par-aamir-returns-to-japanese-theatres.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The upcoming feature will be distributed in Japan under the localized title 'Sitaare! The Miracle Team of Stardust'. The official announcement regarding its Japanese release was made by Geek Pictures on September 25, 2026, generating early buzz for the movie's arrival. 'Sitaare Zameen Par' is directed by R. S. Prasanna. The narrative centers on a compelling storyline: a coach who undertakes the task of mentoring a basketball team composed of adults with disabilities. This thematic focus is expected to resonate with audiences, continuing Khan's tradition of starring in films that combine entertainment with meaningful social commentary.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on the film's promotional activities in Japan leading up to its spring 2027 release.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article faithfully reflects the information provided in the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/aamir-khans-sitaare-zameen-par-heads-to-japan-marks-actors-return-after-nearly-a-decade/articleshow/134523253.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
