     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Stroke Survivor Conquers Kilimanjaro, Sets Two World Records</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Jayshree Vijay Mohan</span> <span>#Mount Kilimanjaro</span> <span>#Stroke Recovery</span> <span>#World Record</span></div>
       <p>Jayshree Vijay Mohan, a mother of two from Chennai, defied immense odds to climb Mount Kilimanjaro, setting two Guinness World Records in the process. In October 2021, a stroke left the left side of her body paralyzed, profoundly changing her life and challenging her ability to perform even basic movements.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/stroke-survivor-conquers-kilimanjaro-sets-two-world-records.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Despite a long and arduous recovery, which included overcoming a fear of heights and relearning to trust her body, Jayshree embarked on an extraordinary journey. Her daughters provided unwavering support, leaving encouraging notes like, &quot;Amma, you can do this.&quot; After rigorous training, and even recovering from an injury just weeks before the climb, Jayshree completed the ascent of Kilimanjaro in September 2025. She achieved the fastest ascent in 5 days, 6 hours, and 50 minutes, and the fastest descent in 10 hours and 26 minutes, both recognized in the CIH (Coordination Impairment–Hemiplegia) female category. Her remarkable achievement stands as a testament to her resilience.</p><p>Why it matters: Jayshree's story inspires others to redefine personal limits and pursue extraordinary goals even after life-altering challenges.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is a faithful, well-structured summary of the provided text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/changemakers/stroke-survivor-mountaineer-jayshree-chennai-mount-kilimanjaro-guinness-world-record-12571848" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
