       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>‘Two-State Solution’ Key To Lasting Israel-Palestine Peace, Jaishankar Says At UNGA</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#India</span> <span>#Palestine</span> <span>#Israel</span> <span>#Two-State Solution</span></div>
       <p>India's External Affairs Minister, S. Jaishankar, recently addressed the United Nations General Assembly (UNGA), emphasizing the critical importance of a 'Two-State Solution' for achieving lasting peace between Israel and Palestine. Jaishankar's remarks reiterated India's consistent stance on the long-standing conflict, highlighting the necessity of a diplomatic resolution that addresses the aspirations of both sides.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/two-state-solution-key-to-lasting-israel-palestine-peace-jai.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During his address, the Minister underscored that a viable and sustainable two-state solution remains the most credible path forward to ensure stability and security in the region. This position aligns with broad international consensus regarding the framework for resolving the Israeli-Palestinian dispute.</p><p>Further demonstrating India's commitment to the region, the Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) confirmed that India has provided substantial humanitarian assistance to Palestinians. Since the onset of the recent conflict, approximately 70 metric tonnes of aid have been dispatched. This provision of humanitarian support underscores India's concern for the well-being of the Palestinian people amidst the ongoing challenges. Jaishankar's statement at the UNGA reinforces India's diplomatic engagement and humanitarian efforts in the context of the Middle East.</p><p>What to watch: Diplomatic efforts at the UN and regional developments concerning the two-state solution.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source material and provides sufficient context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/two-state-solution-key-to-lasting-israel-palestine-peace-jaishankar-says-at-unga-ws-kl-10355183.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
