     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-09-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Virat Kohli breaks Mohammad Azharuddin's 28-year-old record in 1st India vs West Indies ODI</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Virat Kohli</span> <span>#Record</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>In a significant milestone for Indian cricket, star batsman Virat Kohli has surpassed a long-standing record held by former captain Mohammad Azharuddin. Kohli achieved this feat during the first One Day International against West Indies, played in Thiruvananthapuram on September 27, 2026. This particular match marked Kohli's 44th appearance in an ODI against the West Indies.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-27/virat-kohli-breaks-mohammad-azharuddins-28-year-old-record-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Prior to this game, Mohammad Azharuddin held the record for the most ODIs played against the West Indies by an Indian batsman, with 43 matches to his name. This record had stood unchallenged for an impressive 28 years, highlighting the rarity and significance of Kohli's achievement.</p><p>Kohli's consistent presence and enduring form in international cricket have allowed him to reach this landmark, further solidifying his position among the sport's legends. The occasion was observed during a crucial series opener, adding another layer of importance to his career trajectory. His dedication to the game and ability to maintain peak performance over extended periods continue to set new benchmarks.</p><p>What to watch: Kohli's ongoing contributions in the series and his pursuit of further cricketing milestones.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly synthesizes the information from the source provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/virat-kohli-breaks-mohammad-azharuddins-28-year-old-record-in-1st-india-vs-west-indies-odi/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
